Implement user story SKY-004-b: Dashboard HTML and build configuration

## Story Description
Create src/public/index.html as a styled single-page dashboard for flight search, and configure package.json with build/start scripts and devDependencies. The dashboard must have a blue header, centered search form card, search button, status area, and client-side JS calling GET /search. The build script must produce dist/server.js and copy src/public/ to dist/public/ so the dashboard file is available in both dev (tsx) and production (node dist/server.js) modes. The / route handler in server.ts (from SKY-004-a) reads this file at runtime via fs.readFileSync. Depends on SKY-004-a for the server that serves this file.

## Acceptance Criteria
- src/public/index.html exists as a styled single-page dashboard with: full-width solid-color header bar (blue #1a73e8) containing bold white 'Skyscanner Dashboard' title and smaller subtitle; centered white card (max-width ~700px, rounded corners, light border, padding) with 2-column grid search form — row 1: From (IATA) and To (IATA) text inputs with labels, row 2: Date (native date input) and Adults (number input, default 1) with labels; full-width solid-color button (same blue as header) labeled 'Search Flights'; status/message area showing light-red/pink banner with red text for errors, muted-gray line for empty results, and result count on success
- Dashboard includes client-side JavaScript that submits the search form via GET /search without full page reload, disables the search button while the request is in flight, and renders returned flights into a results table (or appropriate status message) in the same page
- package.json contains a 'start' script with value 'node dist/server.js'
- package.json contains a 'build' script (tsup or equivalent) that produces dist/server.js such that `npm run build && npm run start` successfully starts the server and GET /health returns HTTP 200
- package.json 'build' script copies src/public/ into dist/public/ — after `npm run build`, dist/public/index.html exists and GET / serves the real dashboard file (not 404 or hardcoded fallback)
- supertest and @types/supertest are listed in package.json devDependencies
- `npx tsc --noEmit` exits 0 with no type errors





